{
  "rule": "gradient_duo",
  "metric": "Linf",
  "expected_min_order": 0.9,
  "notes": "C-grid normal gradient on a DUO icosahedral triangular mesh: (grad q)_e = (q[faces_on_edge[e,2]] - q[faces_on_edge[e,1]]) / dv_edge[e], the discrete adjoint of divergence_duo (edge OUTPUT from a cell-centered input). MMS: linear scalar q=a·r̂ with a=(1,0.37,-0.6); analytic edge-normal gradient a·n̂_e (circumcenter-chord normal). Over the level 2 -> 3 -> 4 unit-sphere ladder the observed L-inf orders are approximately [0.99, 0.99] (the two-point edge-normal difference is first-order in L-inf on the irregular icosahedral mesh, where the circumcenter chord is not exactly edge-perpendicular at the most distorted cells); we require min order >= 0.9. See Heikes et al. (2023) and the C-grid order analysis in Thuburn et al. (2009)."
}
